comment.narrative:
Projects
- 1 training programme for RAC teachers (10-12), students (25 graduates in 2020) and 100 technicians from the local market;
- 2 workshops for importers (26 importers) and 2 workshops for customs officers (15-20)
- Launching of the HPMP RP for HFCs phase-down funding if approved by the MLF;
- Participate in 2020 MP meeting/conferences (MoP, ExCom & OEWG);
Agreements, Laws, Decrees and Decisions
- Preparation and submission to the Ozone / MLF Secretariats of CP and A7 ODS Data reports (Imports/Consumption) for the year 2019;
- Cooperate with customs and importers to control imports and exports of ODSs through enforcing of the ODS licensing system, technical assistance on new HS codes for HFCs and their blends; Issuance of 2020 quotas of ODSs;
- Issue ministerial decision to ban imports of R-141b use in foam (sandwish panels sector) that will be effective in 2021
Awareness
- Dissemination of the Sun Safe Guidebook to public libraries, schools and NGOs (approx 3000 copies);
- Distribution of 500 RAC sector servicing guidebook to vocational school students, technicians and service workshops;

Project:
- Request for HPMP-Tranche-3 submission to te 86th ExCom meeting for approval of fund release. Submission of IS-XII extension request to the 86th ExCom meeting for funding. 
- Submission of HFCs phase down PRP funding submitted to the 86th ExCom meeting. 

Agreements, Law Decrees and Decisions:
- Submission of the the 2019 CP reports and A7 reports on ODSs consumption and Imports to the MLF secretariat / Ozone secretariat;
- Enforcement of the ODS Licensing system through the close monitoring of the quota of imports for 2020;
- Issuance of quota of HCFCs imports for 2021 ;
- Work with customs initiated for updating the HS codes for HFCs in liaison with World Customs Organization (WCO) and UN Environment West Asia Office;
- Participated in the 42nd OEWG and the ExCom-85th meeting 2020 (Online);
- Decision issued by the Minister for banning imports of R-141b used in RAC systems for flushing/ cleaning purposes;
- Organized a workshop with ODS importers (attendees: 25 importers February 25, 2020).

Projects
- Monitoring the implementation of the training programme for teachers and technicians of RAC sector;
- Organizing 2 workshops for importers (30 importers) and 2 workshops for customs officers (15-20);
- Launching of the HPMP PRP for HFCs phase-down funding if approved by the MLF;
- Participating in 2021 MP meeting/conferences (MoP, ExCom & OEWG).

Agreements, Laws, Decrees and Decisions
- Preparation and submission to the Ozone / MLF Secretariats of CP and A7 ODS Data reports (Imports/Consumption) for the year 2020;
- Cooperate with customs and importers to control imports and exports of ODSs through enforcing of the ODS licensing system, technical assistance on new HS codes for HFCs and their blends; Issuance of 2022 quotas of ODSs;
- Issue ministerial decision to ban imports of R-141b use in foam (sandwich panels sector) that will be effective in January 2021.

Awareness
- Dissemination of the Sun Safe Guidebook to public libraries, schools and NGOs (approx. 2000 copies);
- Distribution of 200 RAC sector servicing guidebook to vocational school students, technicians and service workshops.

Projects 
- Completion of training programme for teachers and technicians at Al-Amal vocational school RAC center; 
- Due to COVID pandemic postponement of the workshops for importers customs officers; 
- Approval of HPMP PRP for HFCs phase-down funding by the MLF at the 87th ExCom meeting ; 
- Participating (Online) in 2021 MP meeting/conferences (MoP, ExCom & OEWG) April, June and July, October and November 2021

Agreements, Laws, Decrees and Decisions 
- Submission to the Ozone / MLF Secretariats of CP and A7 ODS Data reports (Imports/ Consumption) for the year 2020; 
- Submission to the Minister decision to ban imports of R-141b use in all manufacturing enterprises, and the draft decision for amending the ODS licensing system to include HFCs as per the guidelines of Kigali amendment; and the Importers registration decisions and quotas for 2022 (awaiting for Minister endorsement)

Awareness 
- Due to schools shutdown postponement of the dissemination of the Sun Safe Guidebook to public libraries, schools and NGOs

Projects 
- Update the ODS data base for HCFCs and HFCs users in the country; 
- Launching of the ISP project Phase XII and the HPMP PRP for HFCs phase-down strategy project;
- Submission to the MLF secretariat for the release of the HPMP Tranche-4 funds (US$ 260,000) and for funding the HPMP Stage-III (US$ 1.5 M); 
- Submission of reports to the Ozone/MLF Secretariats of the Country- Programme and Article-7 ODS Data reports (Imports/Consumption) for the year 2021;
- Update the National technical assistance plan of the RAC servicing sector; 
- Participate in 2022 MP meetings/conferences (MoP, ExCom & OEWG)

Agreements, Laws, Decrees and Decisions 
- Coordinate with customs and importers to control imports and exports of ODSs through enforcing of the ODS licensing system, technical assistance on new HS codes for HFCs and their blends; Issuance of 2023 quotas of ODSs; 
- Issuance of a Ministerial decision to ban imports of R-141b use in all manufacturing industrial sectors; 
- Amendment of the ODS licensing system to include the control of imports/exports and consumption of HFCs; 
- Follow-up for implementnation of the amendment/upgrade of the BT curriculum in relation to the RAC sector with MEHE/DGVTE and UNICE;
- Coordinate with Minister of Environment on the National Cooling Plan NCP Endorsement and COM approval; 

Awareness 
- Conduct 3 workshops: one for customs and 2 for importers on 
- Dissemination of the remaining quantity of the Sun Safe Guidebook to public libraries, schools and NGOs (approx 2000 copies); 
- Distribution of 200 RAC sector servicing guidebook to Bakhoun vocational school students and teachers;
- Improving kids awareness on being sun safe and protecting the ozone layer through the collaboration with environmental and kids clubs...

Projects
- Launching of the ISP XII and the HPMP PRP for HFCs phase-down projects (July 2022) ; 
- Submission of reports to the Ozone/MLF Secretariats of the Country-Programme and Article-7 ODS data reports (Imports/Consumption) for the year 2021;
- Prepared the strategy plan for training programme for teachers and student as well technicians in the market;
- Completion of the rehabilitation of the RAC center as well training of teachers at Bakhoun vocational school RAC center (3 women attended);
- Participated in 2022 MP meetings: the 89th ExCom (Online), the 90th ExCom (in person), the OEWG meeting (Online), the regional network meeting of West Asia (in person), and MOP 34 (in person), as well to participate in the 91st ExCom meeting in Montreal 4-9 Dec. 2022.

Agreements, Laws, Decrees and Decisions 
- Enforcement of the ODS licensing system including the control of imports of HFCs;
- Ministerial decision 404/1 for the ban of imports of R-141b use in all manufacturing industrial sectors issued; 
- Ministerial decisions issued on the registration of importers and quotas for 2023;
- RAC vocational curriculum upgrade completed

Awareness 
- Organized 2 workshops for importers in January 27, 2022 (On Teams – 11 importer attendees (4 women attended)) and on October 7, 2022 (25 importer attendees (6 women attended)); 
- Dissemination of 1845 copies of the Sun Safe Guidebook;
- Distribution of 100 RAC sector servicing guidebook to Bakhoun vocational school students;
- Kids awareness materials and dissemination were transmitted through the collaboration with NGOs.
